Z||000012||Phantom Rage||11-01-1999||01:49 PM||||Yes that is a chrysler product, If you watch it again, look at the nose of the car and you will see the chrysler symbol, another funny thing is check out some of the other cars, a lot of Mopars.  I had an old article on it, but can't seem to find it.  If I can recall it had a 2.2L Twin turbocharged motor, capable of 400hp.  The other thing I recall was the paint, I think it cost $38,000, yes $38,000 not $3800.  I think PPG helped in the making of this car.||||reg||12
Z||000013||superXmotorsports||11-22-1999||10:46 PM||||Hey everybody - to revive an old topic I met the new owners of the Wraith II project today.  3 of my parts cars are on their way to being 'Wraiths'  They only use the cockpit area of the Fiero and they said they use a GM ZZsomething crate V8 w/ Porsche 914 transaxle.  They also told me that the original Wraith car for the movie (they said it was 6cyl turbo) sold for only $25k through the movie studio.  I'll keep you all posted about the Fiero/Wraith II projects.||||reg||4
